cratic flip, mostly Safe/Solid D", "Polymarket prices Pan near 96% to win", "Pan's outside spending ($1.4M) far exceeds Kiley's outside support"], "rationale": "The newly drawn Sacramento-area seat has a Democratic-leaning baseline, and nine of nine raters call it a Democratic flip, most at Safe or Solid D; markets agree at roughly 96%. Kiley's incumbency and fundraising edge are outweighed by the district's lean and Pan's heavy outside backing.", "watch": "Any late polling showing Kiley running unusually strong among moderates, or a shift in the national House environment toward Republicans, would narrow the expected margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Kevin Kiley (I) is running.", "Kevin Kiley is an independent standing in for the Republican side."]}, "overview": "California's 6th District was redrawn ahead of 2026, putting incumbent Kevin Kiley, running as an independent on the Republican side, into a seat with a five-point Democratic lean. State Senator Richard Pan, a physician known for California's vaccine laws, advanced past the top-two primary and has drawn heavy outside spending support, about $1.4 million, while Kiley holds a large cash-on-hand advantage from his own fundraising.\n\nEvery major race rater rates this a Democratic flip, most calling it Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price Pan near 96%. With no general-election polling available, the forecast rests on the district's fundamentals, the ratings consensus, and market pricing, all pointing to a Democratic pickup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9603, "margin": 11.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.95, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 13.0}]}